{"level":"info","message":"Generated response:","responseText":"It sounds like you've noticed a change in your attention span, and it's completely understandable to feel concerned when something like that shifts. It takes a lot of self-awareness to notice these patterns, and I appreciate you sharing this with me.\n\nMany things can influence our focus and attention, and often it's not just one factor but a combination. Sometimes, things like stress, sleep patterns, how much time we spend with screens, or even general lifestyle habits can play a significant role.\n\nI'm wondering, have you noticed any other changes in your daily life recently that might be contributing to this feeling, or anything that seems to make it better or worse? We could explore some of those potential connections, and then look at practical, evidence-based strategies, like mindfulness or specific attention-focusing exercises, that might help strengthen your cognitive well-being. How does that sound as a next step?","timestamp":"2026-01-01T13:43:30.205Z"}
