{"level":"info","message":"Generated response:","responseText":"I hear you're feeling that your attention span is getting low, and it's completely understandable to feel concerned or even frustrated when you notice changes like that. Many people find their focus fluctuates at different times, and it can definitely impact how we feel day-to-day.\n\nIf you're open to it, we could explore some evidence-based strategies that are often very helpful in strengthening attention and focus. Approaches from cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT) and mindfulness can offer practical ways to better understand and manage distractions, and gently guide your focus back to what's important.\n\nWould you be interested in learning more about some of these techniques, or perhaps by sharing if there are specific situations or tasks where you notice your attention waning the most?","timestamp":"2026-01-01T13:54:19.978Z"}
