{"event":{"data":{"goals":[],"history":[{"_id":"6958c1999f831698319bfd80","content":"i am feeling unhappy","role":"user","timestamp":"2026-01-03T07:13:29.281Z"},{"_id":"6958c1999f831698319bfd81","content":"I'm sorry to hear that you're feeling unhappy right now. It takes courage to express how you're feeling, and I appreciate you sharing that with me. Please know that it's okay to feel this way.\n\nSometimes, just talking about what's on your mind can be a helpful first step. If you feel comfortable, I'm here to listen without judgment. Would you like to tell me a little more about what might be contributing to this feeling, or when you first noticed it? We can explore it together at your own pace.","metadata":{"analysis":{"emotionalState":"unhappy","progressIndicators":["Expression of more specific emotions (e.g., sadness, frustration, loneliness)","Identification of contributing factors or triggers to their unhappiness","Engagement in self-reflection regarding their feelings"],"recommendedApproach":"Exploratory and supportive, focusing on active listening and open-ended questions to understand the source and nature of unhappiness.","riskLevel":0,"themes":["Emotional well-being","Mood regulation"]},"progress":{"emotionalState":"unhappy","riskLevel":0}},"role":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-01-03T07:13:29.286Z"},{"_id":"6958c1d39f831698319bfd93","content":"things arent going as i expected","role":"user","timestamp":"2026-01-03T07:14:27.747Z"},{"_id":"6958c1d39f831698319bfd94","content":"It sounds like you're going through a challenging time right now, and it's completely understandable to feel a sense of disappointment when things aren't unfolding as you had hoped. It takes a lot of courage to acknowledge that.\n\nI'm here to listen. Would you be willing to share a bit more about what \"things\" aren't going as you expected, and what some of those expectations were? We can explore this together.","metadata":{"analysis":{"emotionalState":"Disappointment","progressIndicators":["Clearer articulation of the specific challenges","Identification of core expectations","Openness to exploring alternative perspectives or strategies"],"recommendedApproach":"Empathic validation of the user's feelings, followed by open-ended questions to explore what 'things' are not going as expected and what specific expectations were held.","riskLevel":0,"themes":["Unmet Expectations","Coping with Adversity"]},"progress":{"emotionalState":"Disappointment","riskLevel":0}},"role":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-01-03T07:14:27.748Z"},{"_id":"6958c2279f831698319bfda0","content":"i am feeling so much distracted ,not able to focus properly.Its not like i dont want to do it but my mind refuses","role":"user","timestamp":"2026-01-03T07:15:51.003Z"},{"_id":"6958c2279f831698319bfda1","content":"It sounds really challenging and frustrating when you *want* to focus and engage, but your mind just feels like it's pulling in another direction. It's completely understandable to feel that internal push-and-pull, especially when your intentions are clear, but the execution feels blocked. Many people experience this feeling of their mind \"refusing\" to cooperate, and it can be quite disheartening.\n\nOften, when we feel this strong sense of distraction and an inability to focus, it can be our mind's way of signaling that something else might be at play. Sometimes stress, feeling overwhelmed, or even underlying worries can make it incredibly difficult to settle our thoughts and direct our attention.\n\nWe can explore some practical techniques to help you gently guide your focus back when your mind feels scattered. Would you be open to discussing strategies like breaking down tasks into smaller, more manageable steps, trying a short mindfulness exercise to anchor your attention, or even setting very clear, short-term intentions for your work periods? We can find what might work best for you.","metadata":{"analysis":{"emotionalState":"Frustrated and struggling with focus","progressIndicators":["Reports improved ability to concentrate for sustained periods","Describes fewer instances of feeling 'mind refuses'","Demonstrates increased ability to initiate and complete tasks"],"recommendedApproach":"Acknowledge the user's frustration and the struggle between intention and execution. Explore potential underlying causes for distraction (e.g., stress, cognitive overload, anxiety). Introduce practical strategies for improving focus, such as mindfulness techniques, breaking down tasks, or setting clear intentions for work periods.","riskLevel":0,"themes":["Focus and Attention","Motivation-Action Gap","Cognitive Control"]},"progress":{"emotionalState":"Frustrated and struggling with focus","riskLevel":0}},"role":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-01-03T07:15:51.003Z"},{"_id":"6958c24f9f831698319bfdaf","content":"ok i am all ears","role":"user","timestamp":"2026-01-03T07:16:31.893Z"},{"_id":"6958c24f9f831698319bfdb0","content":"It sounds like you're ready to dive in, and I appreciate you being open to that. To start, what's been on your mind, or what feels most important for us to explore today? There's no right or wrong place to begin.","metadata":{"analysis":{"emotionalState":"Receptive","progressIndicators":["Engagement","Readiness to participate"],"recommendedApproach":"Initiate dialogue or prompt for current thoughts/feelings.","riskLevel":0,"themes":[]},"progress":{"emotionalState":"Receptive","riskLevel":0}},"role":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-01-03T07:16:31.893Z"},{"_id":"6958c31f9f831698319bfdc0","content":"a bit about unconsciousness","role":"user","timestamp":"2026-01-03T07:19:59.944Z"},{"_id":"6958c31f9f831698319bfdc1","content":"That's a really intriguing topic to bring up. It sounds like you're feeling curious about the concept of the unconscious, and it's a profound area that many find themselves drawn to exploring.\n\nThe idea of the unconscious mind is a rich and complex one, and it can offer so many insights into who we are and why we do what we do. It's often where hidden motivations, forgotten memories, and even creative impulses reside, influencing us in ways we might not always consciously recognize.\n\nWhat comes to mind for you when you think about 'unconsciousness,' or what sparked your interest in it today?","metadata":{"analysis":{"emotionalState":"Curious","progressIndicators":["Increased awareness of unconscious influences on thoughts and behaviors","New insights into personal motivations or patterns","Making connections between past experiences and present feelings/actions","Understanding symbolic meanings","Reduced internal conflict or confusion related to inner experiences"],"recommendedApproach":"A psychodynamic or psychoanalytic approach, encouraging exploratory discussion around the nature and influence of the unconscious. Techniques could include free association, dream analysis, and reflecting on recurring patterns or symbols to uncover underlying thoughts and feelings.","riskLevel":0,"themes":["Unconsciousness","Depth Psychology","Self-exploration","Hidden Motivations","Dreams","Symbolism","Psychodynamic Concepts"]},"progress":{"emotionalState":"Curious","riskLevel":0}},"role":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-01-03T07:19:59.944Z"}],"memory":{"sessionContext":{"conversationThemes":[],"currentTechnique":null},"userProfile":{"emotionalState":[],"preferences":{},"riskLevel":0}},"message":"its like getting lost from real world","systemPrompt":"You are an AI therapist assistant. Your role is to:\n        1. Provide empathetic and supportive responses\n        2. Use evidence-based therapeutic techniques\n        3. Maintain professional boundaries\n        4. Monitor for risk factors\n        5. Guide users toward their therapeutic goals"},"name":"therapy/session.message"},"level":"info","message":"Sending message to Inngest:","timestamp":"2026-01-03T15:16:00.148Z"}
