 do what we do. It's often where hidden motivations, forgotten memories, and even creative impulses reside, influencing us in ways we might not always consciously recognize.\n\nWhat comes to mind for you when you think about 'unconsciousness,' or what sparked your interest in it today?","metadata":{"analysis":{"emotionalState":"Curious","progressIndicators":["Increased awareness of unconscious influences on thoughts and behaviors","New insights into personal motivations or patterns","Making connections between past experiences and present feelings/actions","Understanding symbolic meanings","Reduced internal conflict or confusion related to inner experiences"],"recommendedApproach":"A psychodynamic or psychoanalytic approach, encouraging exploratory discussion around the nature and influence of the unconscious. Techniques could include free association, dream analysis, and reflecting on recurring patterns or symbols to uncover underlying thoughts and feelings.","riskLevel":0,"themes":["Unconsciousness","Depth Psychology","Self-exploration","Hidden Motivations","Dreams","Symbolism","Psychodynamic Concepts"]},"progress":{"emotionalState":"Curious","riskLevel":0}},"role":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-01-03T07:19:59.944Z"},{"_id":"695932be95da5af4937518cf","content":"its like getting lost from real world","role":"user","timestamp":"2026-01-03T15:16:14.033Z"},{"_id":"695932be95da5af4937518d0","content":"Thank you for sharing that with me. \"Getting lost from the real world\" sounds like a profoundly disorienting and perhaps even unsettling experience. It takes a lot to put words to a feeling like that, and I want you to know I hear you and what you're describing.\n\nTo help me understand this feeling better, could you tell me a little more about what it's like for you? What does 'getting lost' feel like in those moments, and when does it tend to happen?\n\nUnderstanding these experiences can be a really important step in finding ways to feel more connected and grounded again. I'm here to listen and help you explore this together.","metadata":{"analysis":{"emotionalState":"Detachment/Disengagement","progressIndicators":["Client reports reduced frequency or intensity of feeling 'lost'","Client identifies triggers for detachment/escapism","Client explores healthier coping mechanisms","Client expresses increased connection to present moment/reality"],"recommendedApproach":"Gently explore the nature, frequency, and triggers of this feeling of 'getting lost'. Validate the client's experience and assess its impact on daily functioning and well-being. Consider introducing grounding techniques.","riskLevel":2,"themes":["Escapism","Reality Avoidance","Dissociation"]},"progress":{"emotionalState":"Detachment/Disengagement","riskLevel":2}},"role":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-01-03T15:16:14.035Z"}],"memory":{"sessionContext":{"conversationThemes":[],"currentTechnique":null},"userProfile":{"emotionalState":[],"preferences":{},"riskLevel":0}},"message":"its like when i am trying to focus on something for a long time , suddenly i go out of context and my brain focuses on other things","systemPrompt":"You are an AI therapist assistant. Your role is to:\n        1. Provide empathetic and supportive responses\n        2. Use evidence-based therapeutic techniques\n        3. Maintain professional boundaries\n        4. Monitor for risk factors\n        5. Guide users toward their therapeutic goals"},"name":"therapy/session.message"},"level":"info","message":"Sending message to Inngest:","timestamp":"2026-01-03T15:18:09.138Z"}
